:false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-05-15T10:35:38Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T17:28:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- 4.6.2\n- 4.7-beta-2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta2 - 'Gentoo' '2.18' on Tty - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 3GB (nvidia; 580.95.05) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-2600 CPU @ 3.40GHz (8 threads) - 31.32 Gio memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nA given mesh instance with a size of 24x24x24, is not occluded as expected. This happen when the said box is too close of the occluder.\n\n<img width=\"1622\" height=\"760\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5dc59f2f-7cd5-4b1a-bb5e-a2c498c88ba6\" />\n\nThis is an issue in production because I have many MultimeshInstance3D with custom AABB that are not occluded when it should. These MultiMeshInstance3D hold a lot of things and should not be rendered if not necessary. In the screen shot below, a lot of chunks should be occluded.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1031\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e3cf343-84a2-42ac-93f4-c1e0f8f9df8c\" />\n\nWorst case scenario is when, from far away, Mesh box are not occluded at all anymore\n\n<img width=\"1619\" height=\"637\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3ffb62ac-989c-483f-a5cd-8f6097f90433\" />\n\nLet me know If I missed a point or If I'm not used using occlusion culling the right way.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the MRP, from the editor, you can move around the camera. The bug is quickly triggered with many kind of camera angles.\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[wrong-occlusing-culling.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27796955/wrong-occlusing-culling.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119488/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}